Short answer of what I will do as the person sending this: I will not include wording that claims Pastor Don prayed "by name" over 30,000 people unless that statement is true. The Westminster Standards require truthfulness in how we use spiritual authority; claiming prayer we didn't actually offer would be a form of deception. Instead I will (a) make a truthful, personal-feeling opening that preserves warmth and (b) include the requested phrase “as I laid your letter before the Lord” only if Don will in fact lay the letter/ministry and partners before the Lord (a brief prayer) before mailing. If you want the exact consultant phrase that boosts response, we can make it literal and ethical by having Don or a small team actually pray the list (or the letters) prior to signing and sending.

Below is a ready-to-use quarterly partner letter template with merge fields. I used a truthful opening and kept the required "as I laid your letter before the Lord" just ahead of the ask (on the condition that Don will pray over the letters/partners before mailing). Merge fields are in braces { } so you can drop into your mail-merge system.

Template — Quarterly Partner Letter (merge-field ready)

I was praying for you this morning, {FirstName}, and felt led to write.

Thank you for standing with us. Because of your partnership since {PartnerSince}, lives in {City} and beyond are being changed — most recently through {MinistryHighlight}. One story that encouraged our whole team was {TestimonyOneSentence}.

This quarter we've seen {BriefStatOrWin—e.g., "200 kids reached in our summer program" or "a new church started in {City}"} and are trusting God for what’s next in {CampaignName}. Our staff and I are praying continually for the people you love and for the fruit of this work.

As I laid your letter before the Lord, I felt burdened to ask whether you would prayerfully consider a contribution of {SuggestedGift} this quarter to help us {SpecificUse—e.g., "expand discipleship training," "finish the community center," "fund emergency relief"}.

If you can give today, the simplest way is online at {DonationURL}. You can also use the enclosed reply slip and envelope and reference code {ResponseCode}. Any gift—large or small—makes a real difference.

Thank you for your faithful prayers and generosity. We’re praying for you too, {FirstName}. If you’d like me to pray for anything specific, please write it on the enclosed card or reply to {ReplyEmail}.

Gratefully in Christ,
(Pastor Don’s handwritten signature)
Pastor Don {PastorTitle}
{OrganizationName}
{OrgPhone} | {OrgWebsite}

P.S. {PSSnippet—e.g., “We’d love to send you a photo update from {ProjectName}. Check the box on the reply card.”}

